>> title: Madeleines
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: butter, lemon, french, teatime, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: madeleine, French butter cakes, shell cakes
>> servings: 18
>> time: 1 hour 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the hump comes from cold batter meeting a hot tin and nothing else, so the hour in the fridge is not a rest you can skip
>> step.6: fold in the butter

Butter and flour a #madeleine pan{}.

Heat the #oven{} to 375°F (190°C).

Whisk @eggs{2%large}(100 g) with @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g), @honey{1%Tbs}(21 g), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL), and @lemon zest{1%tsp}(2 g).

Whisk @all-purpose flour{3/4%cup}(95 g), @baking powder{1/2%tsp}(2.4 g), and @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

Fold @&(~1)dry ingredients{} into @&(~2)egg mixture{}.

Fold @melted butter{1/2%cup}(113 g; cooled) into @&(~1)batter{}.

Cover @&(~1)batter{} and chill for ~{1%hour}.

Bake @&(~1)batter{} in the pan at 375°F for ~{10%min}.
